'''Vane''' was a [[Gender|male]]<ref name="Arrr" /> [[Kajain'sa'Nikto]] [[pirate]] who was a member of [[Gorian Shard]]'s [[Gorian Shard's pirate crew|gang]]<ref name="Chapter 17" /> as the second-in-command.<ref name="Arrr">{{SW|url=news/who-are-the-pirates-of-the-new-republic|text=Who Arrrrr the Pirates in the New Republic?}}</ref> During the [[pirate siege on Nevarro]], Vane deserted Shard to save his own skin.

==Biography==
===Confrontation on Nevarro===
[[File:Vane_and_crew.png|thumb|left|270px|Vane tries to enter the Nevarro school]]
Vane was considered one of the most famous [[pirate]]s in [[the galaxy]], stories about Vane were shared by members of the [[Hunters of the Outer Rim]] tournament on [[Vespaara]].<ref name="Hunters">{{HuntersCite|quest=Join the Crew}}</ref>

While on the [[Volcano|volcanic]] [[planet]] [[Nevarro]], he along with the other pirates tried to enter a [[Nevarro school|school]] to drink which started a commotion. [[Greef Karga]] and [[Din Djarin]] shortly [[Showdown on Nevarro|confronted]] Vane and the other pirates. Vane and his [[Vane's Snub Fighter squadron|squadron]] attempted to shoot Djarin's [[Din Djarin's N-1 starfighter|starfighter]] down for killing several of his men. Despite losing more men, Vane was able to drive Djarin toward Captain [[Gorian Shard]]'s [[Gorian Shard's pirate Corsair|Corsair]]. However, Djarin was able to escape.<ref name="Chapter 17" />

===Pirate Siege===
[[File:Vane_decides_to_flee.png|thumb|right|270px|Vane fleeing from the battle]]
Vane, along with [[Gorian Shard]] and the rest of the gang returned to Nevarro and took [[Pirate siege on Nevarro|control]] of [[Nevarro City]]. Vane and his squadron were then sent to take care of Djarin when he attacked Shard's ship. As Vane and his squadron chased Djarin, they came under attack by [[Lady]] [[Bo-Katan Kryze]] in her [[Bo-Katan Kryze's Gauntlet starfighter|fighter]] while [[The Tribe|their Mandalorian tribe]] engaged pirates on the ground. In response, Vane abandoned Shard's gang and fled.<ref name="Ch. 21">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 21: The Pirate}}</ref>

===Working with Silvo===
[[File:PaxMutiny-SC1.png|thumb|left|270px|Vane joins mutiny against Captain Silvo]]
Sometime after abandoning Shard, Vane decided to work for Captain [[Jod Na Nawood|Silvo]] and his [[Silvo's pirates|pirates]] during a [[Silvo's pirate raid|raid on a New Republic freighter]]. After discovering that all the freighter contained was one [[Credit]], Vane joined [[Brutus]]' mutiny against their captain.<ref name="SC1">{{SkeletonCrew|This Could Be a Real Adventure}}</ref> Vane later found a group of children at [[Borgo Prime]] who claimed to be from [[At Attin]].<ref name="Way, Way Out" /> Later, Vane is present when Brutus is about to execute Silvo, but the former captain convinces his former crew that he can lead them to At Attin's treasure.<ref name="SC6">{{SkeletonCrew|Zero Friends Again}}</ref> Soon after, when Silvo killed Brutus and retook his place of captain, Vane later returned to his former captain.<ref name="SC7">{{SkeletonCrew|We're Gonna Be In So Much Trouble}}</ref>

==Behind the scenes==
Vane first appeared in the [[Chapter 17: The Apostate|first episode]] of the [[The Mandalorian Season Three|third season]] of the [[Disney+]] live-action series ''[[Star Wars: The Mandalorian]]'',<ref name="Chapter 17" /> which aired on [[March 1]], [[2023]].<ref name="Tweet">{{Twitter|starwars|status/1598416900689743873|[[Star Wars]]|date=2022-12-1|quote=The Mandalorian and Grogu return March 1 only on @DisneyPlus.|archiveurl=https://archive.ph/ytQHE}}</ref> The character was portrayed by [[Marti Matulis]].<ref name="Chapter 17" />

Vane was initially meant to [[Death|die]] in the shootout on Nevarro, however [[Jon Favreau]] liked the character and Matulis's portrayal, and chose to keep him alive.<ref name="Interview">{{TOMCite|117|Marti Matulis: Der Mann hinter der Maske}}</ref>

